cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the derived tables, please cite this repository. Author names are withheld while the accompanying manuscript is under double-blind review."
title: "rst-window-audit: reproducibility package for a CITES RST three-year window audit"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, frozen aggregate tables and figures for an audit of the 2026
  CITES Review of Significant Trade three-year sharp-increase window. The
  package rebuilds the exporter x taxon panel from the official CITES Trade
  Database, constructs one-year and three-year sharp-increase labels, fits a
  rule-feature-excluded rolling-origin ranking model, verifies divergence
  cases against raw records, and compares window and threshold arms on a fixed
  candidate list. Raw CITES records are not redistributed.
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous Authors"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-05"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - CITES
  - Review of Significant Trade
  - sharp increase
  - policy audit
  - reproducibility
  - wildlife trade
type: software
